      "ref": "05-academic-papers/open-access-books/d2l/linear-classification-environment-and-distribution-shift.txt",
      "text": "If the distribution can shift in arbitrary ways, then our setup permits the pathological case in which the distribution over inputs remains constant: $p_S(\\mathbf{x}) = p_T(\\mathbf{x})$, but the labels are all flipped: $p_S(y \\mid \\mathbf{x}) = 1 - p_T(y \\mid \\mathbf{x})$."
     }
    ],
